  "summary": {
    "en": {
      "caveats": "The framework's practical utility and performance remain to be validated in real-world deployments, as the study is based on literature synthesis and expert consultation.",
      "what": "The study presents a standardized Digital Twin (DT) design framework for transport system decarbonization by adapting the ISO-23247 manufacturing standard to the transport sector. The framework was developed by combining a systematic literature review of over 100 studies with a Delphi consultation of 10 experts from three UK research institutions, analyzing more than 10,000 data records. The resulting layered architecture spans road, rail, marine, and air transport, organizing systems into observable, communication, control, user, and cross-system entities.",
      "why": "It provides the first unified, scalable reference architecture that translates industrial manufacturing standards to the transport sector, moving beyond fragmented, function-specific use cases toward interoperable, system-level digital twins aligned with climate policy."
